# Comments

Comment **why**, not what the next line already says. Prefer a clear name over a narrating comment.

## Language

Write comments in **English**, same as existing service JSDoc (`maskForeignTerm`, etc.). Learner-facing copy in UI stays Ukrainian.

## What to comment

- Exported functions and public types: a short JSDoc (`/** ... */`) when the name is not enough.
- Non-obvious invariants: why history is filtered by exercise type, why a streak is 2, why Relearning round-robins.
- Domain mapping that lives in code, not in the type name (`WordState.Learning` → Native MC then Foreign MC).
- `@deprecated` when leaving a compat alias.

Do **not** comment:

- Restating the signature (`// returns the exercise type`).
- Every `case` in a trivial switch (Mature → InputFullWord is obvious).
- TODO without an owner or next step.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — narrates the code
// Filter history by exercise
const ofType = history.filter((entry) => entry.exercise === exercise);

// ✅ GOOD — explains the invariant
/** Last N answers of this exercise type, not global consecutiveCorrect. */
function hasConsecutiveCorrectStreak(...) { ... }
```

```ts
// ❌ BAD
// Increment i
i += 1;

// ✅ GOOD
// Skip the first two letters so the stem stays visible (dw_r_e_).
if (index < 2) return char;
```
